{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b1f2a3c4-1234-4a5b-9c6d-host000000001",
    "name": "TriloPlan Host API",
    "description": "Backend API surface for the Host app only — every endpoint a Host-app screen (Figma review, Host app design follow-up) actually calls. Split out of the old single combined collection so each frontend team has its own collection scoped to what it needs. See CLAUDE.md, BACKEND_PLAN.md and BRD.md in the repo for full backend context.\n\nCompanion collections: `TriloPlan-User.postman_collection.json` (seeded with what's built for the User role so far) and `TriloPlan-Admin.postman_collection.json` (everything under `/admin/*`).\n\n## OTP login while there's no real SMS yet\nThe backend has a dev-only bypass (`OTP_BYPASS_VERIFICATION=true` in the server's `.env`, off in production): `POST /auth/otp/verify` accepts ANY phone + ANY 6-digit code, no prior `/otp/request` call required. This collection still calls `/otp/request` first and saves `devCode` (harmless either way), then verifies with it — swap in any 6 digits and it still works while the bypass is on.\n\n## Two identities in this collection\nSeveral Host flows need a counterpart USER to have already done something (called, chatted, gifted) before the Host side has anything to act on — so this collection also logs in a throwaway USER identity in the **Setup** folder purely to drive that, kept separate from the main `hostAccessToken` identity under test. A minimal **Admin — KYC Approval** step is included too, since `Withdrawals` needs the host's KYC approved first (BR-EARN-03) and that's an admin action — same dependency the original combined collection had.\n\n## Recommended run order (Collection Runner-safe, top to bottom)\nSetup → Auth — Host Login → Profile (Me) → Presence → Admin — KYC Approval → Calls → Chat → Gifts → Live Broadcasting → Withdrawals → Earnings → Moderation → Auth — Session.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
  "event": [],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userPhone", "value": "+919876510001", "type": "string", "description": "Counterpart USER identity (Setup folder) used to drive calls/chat/gifts toward the host under test." },
    { "key": "userDevCode", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userAccessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "hostPhone", "value": "+919876510555", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "hostDevCode", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "hostAccessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "hostRefreshToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "hostId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminEmail", "value": "admin@triloplan.com", "type": "string", "description": "Must match an already-seeded ADMIN account (`npm run db:seed-admin -- <phone> <email> <password>`)." },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "ChangeMe123!", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminAccessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "kycUploadUrl", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "kycDocumentKey", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "galleryItemId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "payoutMethodId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "callId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "chatConversationId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "giftId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "liveBroadcastId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "withdrawalId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "reportId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Setup — Counterpart User",
      "description": "A throwaway USER identity, funded with wallet balance, purely so the Host flows below (accept a call, receive a chat message/gift, rate someone) have something real to act on.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Request OTP — Counterpart User",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{userPhone}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/request", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "otp", "request"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.devCode) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"userDevCode\", jsonData.devCode); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Verify OTP — Counterpart User",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{userPhone}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{userDevCode}}\",\n  \"role\": \"user\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/verify", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "otp", "verify"] },
            "description": "Any 6-digit code works while OTP_BYPASS_VERIFICATION is on. Saves userAccessToken/userId."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"userAccessToken\", jsonData.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"userId\", jsonData.user.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Dev-Credit Counterpart User's Wallet",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{userAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"amountPaise\": 500000\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/wallet/dev-credit", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["wallet", "dev-credit"] },
            "description": "Non-prod escape hatch (no payment gateway wired up yet) — funds ₹5,000 so the counterpart user can call/gift the host under test."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth — Host Login",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Request OTP — Host Phone",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{hostPhone}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/request", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "otp", "request"] },
            "description": "Matches the app's \"Your number / Send code\" screen."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.devCode) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"hostDevCode\", jsonData.devCode); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Verify OTP — Host App",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phone\": \"{{hostPhone}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{hostDevCode}}\",\n  \"role\": \"host\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/otp/verify", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "otp", "verify"] },
            "description": "Matches the app's \"Verify number / Enter the code\" screen. Any 6-digit code works while OTP_BYPASS_VERIFICATION is on — creates a new HOST account on first-ever verify for this phone."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"hostAccessToken\", jsonData.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"hostRefreshToken\", jsonData.refreshToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"hostId\", jsonData.user.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Profile (Me)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get My Profile",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me"] },
            "description": "Profile screen header (avatar, @handle, rating, calls) — hostProfile now includes `rating: {average, count}`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update My Profile",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Ayesha\",\n  \"email\": \"host@mail.com\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me"] },
            "description": "Edit profile screen's name/email fields."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Host Profile — Bio, Gallery, Rates, Toggles",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"bio\": \"Late night chats, music and good vibes\",\n  \"ratePerMinutePaise\": 2400,\n  \"voiceRatePerMinutePaise\": 1200,\n  \"privateLiveRatePerMinutePaise\": 3000,\n  \"autoAcceptCalls\": true,\n  \"voiceCallsOnlyAfterMidnight\": false\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/host-profile", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "host-profile"] },
            "description": "Rate Settings screen's \"Save rates\" action — video/voice/private-live per-minute rates (paise) plus the two availability toggles. Must be called before Calls (below) can succeed — a call needs the relevant per-type rate set."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1. Get KYC Upload URL",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"contentType\": \"application/pdf\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/kyc/upload-url", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "kyc", "upload-url"] },
            "description": "\"Upload documents\" screen. Saves kycUploadUrl/kycDocumentKey."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"kycUploadUrl\", jsonData.uploadUrl);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"kycDocumentKey\", jsonData.key);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Upload Document to S3",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/pdf", "type": "text" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "This is placeholder file content for testing the upload flow." },
            "url": { "raw": "{{kycUploadUrl}}", "host": ["{{kycUploadUrl}}"] },
            "description": "Goes straight to S3 with the presigned URL from step 1 — no Authorization header needed."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Submit KYC Document",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"documents\": [\n    { \"documentType\": \"id_front\", \"key\": \"{{kycDocumentKey}}\" }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/kyc", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "kyc"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Get My KYC Status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/kyc", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "kyc"] },
            "description": "\"Under review\" / \"Verified\" / \"Verification rejected\" screens."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add Gallery Item",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"mediaType\": \"photo\",\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/photo.jpg\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/host-profile/gallery", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "host-profile", "gallery"] },
            "description": "Gallery screen's \"+\" tile."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(201); });",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"galleryItemId\", jsonData.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List My Gallery",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/host-profile/gallery", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "host-profile", "gallery"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete Gallery Item",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/host-profile/gallery/{{galleryItemId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["me", "host-profile", "gallery", "{{galleryItemId}}"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "1. Add Payout Method — Bank (Primary)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"type\": \"bank\",\n  \"accountHolderName\": \"Ayesha Khan\",\n  \"accountNumber\": \"1234567894821\",\n  \"ifsc\": \"HDFC0001234\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/payout-methods", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "payout-methods"] },
            "description": "\"Add New Payout Account\" screen — the first payout method added becomes primary automatically."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Add Payout Method — UPI (Backup)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"type\": \"upi\",\n  \"vpa\": \"ayesha@upi\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/payout-methods", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "payout-methods"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(201); });",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"payoutMethodId\", jsonData.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. List Payout Methods",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/payout-methods", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "payout-methods"] },
            "description": "Payout details screen — primary bank account + backup UPI."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Set Primary Payout Method",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/payout-methods/{{payoutMethodId}}/primary",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["me", "payout-methods", "{{payoutMethodId}}", "primary"]
            },
            "description": "Left as the UPI method being promoted — reverted implicitly by not running again, since Withdrawals below just needs *a* primary method on file, either works."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Notification Preferences",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/notification-preferences", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "notification-preferences"] },
            "description": "Notification Settings screen — defaults match the toggle states shown in the design."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Notification Preferences",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"callReminders\": true,\n  \"weeklyEarningsSummary\": true,\n  \"dndEnabled\": false\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/notification-preferences", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "notification-preferences"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Presence",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Go Online",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"isOnline\": true\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/me/presence", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["me", "presence"] },
            "description": "Home screen's \"Go online\" toggle. Must be online before the counterpart user can call this host."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Admin — KYC Approval (dependency)",
      "description": "Minimal cross-cutting dependency: Withdrawals below requires this host's KYC to already be approved (BR-EARN-03), and only an admin can do that.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Admin Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/admin/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "admin", "login"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (jsonData.accessToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set(\"adminAccessToken\", jsonData.accessToken); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Approve This Host's KYC",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"decision\": \"approve\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/kyc/{{hostId}}/decision", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["admin", "kyc", "{{hostId}}", "decision"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Calls",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. (User) Initiate Call → This Host",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{userAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"hostId\": \"{{hostId}}\",\n  \"type\": \"video\"\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/calls", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["calls"] },
            "description": "Run by the counterpart user so the host has an incoming call to accept — matches the \"Incoming video call\" screen from the host's side."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(201); });",
                  "var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"callId\", jsonData.callId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Accept Call",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/calls/{{callId}}/accept", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["calls", "{{callId}}", "accept"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Get Call",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/calls/{{callId}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["calls", "{{callId}}"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "4. End Call",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/calls/{{callId}}/end", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["calls", "{{callId}}", "end"] },
            "description": "\"Call ended\" screen's summary numbers come from this response."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Submit Rating",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{hostAccessToken}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"stars\": 5\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/calls/{{callId}}/rating", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["calls", "{{callId}}", "rating"] },
